{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/GPS Jamming.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/GPS Jamming.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"gps jamming gps jamming","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/GPS Jamming.md","fileName":"GPS Jamming.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"GPS Jamming","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-21 00:56\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[GPS Accuracy Integrity and Resilience]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["GPS Accuracy Integrity and Resilience","gps.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/GPS Jamming.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/GPS Jamming.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"gps jamming gps jamming","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/GPS Jamming.md","fileName":"GPS Jamming.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"GPS Jamming","heading":"GPS Jamming","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"GPS jamming overwhelms the weak satellite signal at a receiver with stronger radio energy in or near the navigation band. Spread-spectrum correlation provides processing gain, but the signals arrive below the ordinary noise floor after traveling from medium Earth orbit, so a nearby low-cost transmitter can deny service over a useful area. Detection, adaptive filtering, protected signals, directional antennas, and independent navigation methods reduce the effect without eliminating the underlying power imbalance.","tags":["baby"],"links":["GPS Accuracy Integrity and Resilience","gps.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/GPS Jamming.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/GPS Jamming.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"gps jamming gps jamming","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/GPS Jamming.md","fileName":"GPS Jamming.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"GPS Jamming","heading":"Referenc